formed part of religious knowledge.", "Pondok. Students studied the Quran, hadith and Arabic. Pondok subjects should be distinguished from those of other institutions.", "Madrasah. Learning had a syllabus, classes and levels of study. Madrasah learning was organised through classes and levels.", "The palace. Learning also covered administration and the political system. Do not assume every place of learning taught identical subjects."], "text": "The nature of education. Formal education in Malay society emphasised Islamic studies. Learning settings had different areas of emphasis. Mosques and surau. Studies included tajwid, hadith, Islamic jurisprudence and theology. These studies formed part of religious knowledge. Pondok. Students studied the Quran, hadith and Arabic. Pondok subjects should be distinguished from those of other institutions. Madrasah. Learning had a syllabus, classes and levels of study. Madrasah learning was organised through classes and levels. The palace. Learning also covered administration and the political system. Do not assume every place of learning taught identical subjects."}